# Realign the vehicle local-position estimate to a reference pose.
#
# `pose` provides an optional reference for the realignment. Implementations
# that support it use `pose` as the target state; implementations that do not
# (e.g. PiHawk companion-link bridge, which recalculates an OptiTrack-to-FCU
# local-frame offset from current live readings) may ignore `pose` and derive
# the target state from current sensor data. Callers should not rely on `pose`
# being honoured unless the platform documents support for it.
#
# Implementations must reject while the vehicle is armed or actively flying
# unless the platform documents a safe in-flight policy for small-offset
# realignments.
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pose
---
bool success
string message  # human-readable result or rejection reason
